WEBVTT

00:00:01.669 --> 00:00:03.462
<i>(IF I HAD A HEART</i> PLAYING)

00:01:12.907 --> 00:01:14.241
-(ARROW WHOOSHING)

00:01:12.907 --> 00:01:14.241
-(VASE SHATTERING)

00:01:16.118 --> 00:01:17.912
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:01:17.954 --> 00:01:20.832
KALF: That was impressive.

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.416
I modified

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.416
the Frankish weapon.

00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:24.460
It has a much

00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:24.460
greater range now.

00:01:24.502 --> 00:01:26.337
The Franks will not expect

00:01:24.502 --> 00:01:26.337
to be attacked

00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:27.672
-by their own weapon.

00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:27.672
-(LAGERTHA IN NATIVE TONGUE)

00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:28.923
Freyr, we summon you.

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:30.090
(CHANTING)

00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:31.467
We summon you.

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:32.802
(CHANTING CONTINUES)

00:01:32.844 --> 00:01:34.971
With the blood

00:01:32.844 --> 00:01:34.971
of this sacrifice,

00:01:32.844 --> 00:01:34.971
now is the time.

00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:36.055
ALL: Ahhh!

00:01:36.931 --> 00:01:38.098
(WEAPONS CLINKING)

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:40.685
Bjorn must have

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:40.685
murdered our Berserker.

00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:42.770
It's a pity.

00:01:42.812 --> 00:01:44.563
It doesn't matter.

00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:46.774
Really? How can you say so?

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:49.485
Because we have eyes

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:49.485
in Ragnar's household.

00:01:49.527 --> 00:01:52.154
Anything we need

00:01:49.527 --> 00:01:52.154
to know, we'll find out.

00:01:52.196 --> 00:01:54.323
Bjorn's weakness.

00:01:52.196 --> 00:01:54.323
Ragnar's weakness.

00:01:54.365 --> 00:01:55.992
The time to strike.

00:01:56.034 --> 00:01:58.786
-Through Torvi?

00:01:56.034 --> 00:01:58.786
-Of course through Torvi.

00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:00.120
Otherwise,

00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:00.120
I'll kill her child.

00:02:00.162 --> 00:02:02.040
She knows I'll do it, too!

00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:04.667
(GRUNTS)

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:07.127
-(WEAPONS CLINKING)

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:07.127
-(GRUNTS)

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:09.380
WOMAN: (IN DISTANCE) Ahhh!

00:02:09.421 --> 00:02:11.173
Lagertha must never

00:02:09.421 --> 00:02:11.173
know what we did.

00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:13.133
(STRUGGLING)

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:17.722
Who would tell her? Hmm?

00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:24.395
What were you

00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:24.395
two talking about?

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:27.147
Erlendur was telling me

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:27.147
how he has forgiven

00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:27.147
Torvi for leaving him.

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:30.735
-Really?

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:30.735
-Hmm.

00:02:34.113 --> 00:02:36.240
LAGERTHA: That young man

00:02:34.113 --> 00:02:36.240
still surprises me sometimes.

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:41.412
I, too, have a surprise.

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:47.668
I am with child.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.420
(CHUCKLES)

00:02:51.923 --> 00:02:53.424
That makes me so very happy.

00:02:53.465 --> 00:02:54.508
Me too.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.719
More than I can say.

00:02:58.054 --> 00:02:59.680
Although it is

00:02:58.054 --> 00:02:59.680
still early days.

00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:02.850
Marry me, Lagertha.

00:03:03.893 --> 00:03:05.185
Marry me.

00:03:03.893 --> 00:03:05.185
I have always known

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:07.063
that we were fated

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:07.063
to be together.

00:03:07.105 --> 00:03:08.981
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:03:09.648 --> 00:03:11.067
Lagertha?

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.864
-I'm sorry.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.864
-Don't be sorry.

00:03:18.657 --> 00:03:20.409
Don't ever be sorry.

00:03:20.451 --> 00:03:22.161
Say that you'll marry me.

00:03:26.457 --> 00:03:28.375
-(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:03:26.457 --> 00:03:28.375
-(BIRDS CHIRPING)

00:03:33.131 --> 00:03:34.256
Who is he?

00:03:35.591 --> 00:03:36.717
(SIGHS) You heard.

00:03:36.759 --> 00:03:38.343
He's a king.

00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:41.013
From Tamdrup,

00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:41.013
wherever that is.

00:03:41.806 --> 00:03:43.057
And you trust him?

00:03:43.474 --> 00:03:44.433
No!

00:03:45.643 --> 00:03:47.227
I don't trust him either.

00:03:49.855 --> 00:03:52.232
(THUDDING)

00:03:52.274 --> 00:03:55.653
Why do you not care

00:03:52.274 --> 00:03:55.653
for your daughter Siggy?

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:57.071
-MAN: Bring some more

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:57.071
of the shields.

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:57.071
-(BOAT CREAKING)

00:03:57.113 --> 00:03:59.615
I care for her.

00:03:59.657 --> 00:04:01.909
She just reminds me

00:03:59.657 --> 00:04:01.909
of things I'd rather forget.

00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:04.162
What kind of man

00:04:04.203 --> 00:04:05.788
takes a mother

00:04:04.203 --> 00:04:05.788
away from her child?

00:04:07.289 --> 00:04:08.373
(ROPE THUDDING)

00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:10.960
You tell me.

00:04:12.294 --> 00:04:14.130
You tried to take me

00:04:12.294 --> 00:04:14.130
away from my mother.

00:04:16.007 --> 00:04:17.883
That is not the way it went.

00:04:19.051 --> 00:04:21.762
If you remember,

00:04:19.051 --> 00:04:21.762
your mother left me.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.809
You left me.

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:37.736
It is not easy being a father.

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:39.363
It is even harder

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:39.363
being a husband.

00:04:41.532 --> 00:04:43.283
Maybe I have failed at both.

00:04:46.537 --> 00:04:47.663
No.

00:04:47.705 --> 00:04:49.790
VIKING 1: I need a bit more

00:04:47.705 --> 00:04:49.790
slack on the sail.

00:04:49.832 --> 00:04:52.001
(WHISPERS) I have definitely

00:04:49.832 --> 00:04:52.001
failed at being a husband.

00:04:53.044 --> 00:04:54.795
-(CHUCKLES)

00:04:53.044 --> 00:04:54.795
-VIKING 2: Need a hand?

00:04:54.837 --> 00:04:56.130
VIKING 1: Take more than that.

00:04:57.048 --> 00:04:58.298
VIKING 2: No, three will do.

00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:02.678
-VIKING 1: Bring it here.

00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:02.678
-Where do you think?

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.805
-HARALD: I want that

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.805
close to me.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.805
-(PADDLES THUDDING)

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:07.266
VIKING 3: Why would we?

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:08.308
VIKING 1: Oil these oars!

00:05:09.518 --> 00:05:11.478
How many boats and

00:05:09.518 --> 00:05:11.478
men do you have?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.605
WOMAN: More?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.605
No, take more.

00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:15.357
Take one more.

00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:15.357
I will go get one.

00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:15.357
Do you have enough?

00:05:15.399 --> 00:05:16.316
Twenty boats.

00:05:17.776 --> 00:05:19.237
About 600 men.

00:05:21.072 --> 00:05:24.158
I told Ragnar

00:05:21.072 --> 00:05:24.158
mine is a small kingdom

00:05:25.117 --> 00:05:27.036
for now.

00:05:27.078 --> 00:05:27.828
VIKING 1:

00:05:27.078 --> 00:05:27.828
Better for the night.

00:05:29.247 --> 00:05:30.873
And when will they arrive?

00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:34.210
They must already

00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:34.210
be on their way.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.338
My brother Halfdan

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.338
is bringing them.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.631
VIKING 3: Bring him on board.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.631
Can you fill these?

00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:40.883
Is your brother like you?

00:05:41.592 --> 00:05:42.927
No.

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:45.721
He's much worse.

00:05:45.763 --> 00:05:46.722
(LAUGHING)

00:05:48.682 --> 00:05:51.018
(LAUGHING) He's much worse.

00:05:51.894 --> 00:05:53.645
You have such ambitions.

00:05:54.521 --> 00:05:57.024
What else is there?

00:05:57.066 --> 00:06:01.361
What are we here for

00:05:57.066 --> 00:06:01.361
except to achieve fame,

00:05:57.066 --> 00:06:01.361
just like your father?

00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:06.366
Isn't that what

00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:06.366
you want too, Bjorn Lothbrok?

00:06:07.201 --> 00:06:08.452
Be honest.

00:06:08.493 --> 00:06:09.620
You don't know me.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.957
And fame

00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:15.500
won't make

00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:15.500
your small kingdom any bigger.

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:31.850
SENTRY: Rider!

00:06:35.104 --> 00:06:37.106
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:06:37.148 --> 00:06:38.482
WOMAN: How many are there?

00:06:38.523 --> 00:06:40.525
-(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

00:06:38.523 --> 00:06:40.525
-(SWORDS CLINKING)

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.403
Open the gates!

00:06:48.993 --> 00:06:50.369
ECBERT: Werferth.

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:56.334
We are met to decide

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:56.334
how to deal with Mercia.

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:59.003
Now, I am almost decided

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:59.003
that the only way now

00:06:59.044 --> 00:07:01.213
is a full-scale invasion

00:07:01.255 --> 00:07:03.341
of their kingdom.

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:08.595
And, yet, if there were some

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:08.595
other way of restoring Queen

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:08.595
Kwenthrith to her throne,

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:10.472
I think we must explore it.

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:14.893
Have you any more

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:14.893
idea of the identity of

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:14.893
the nobleman you knew as "W"?

00:07:14.935 --> 00:07:17.146
Let me help you please, Sire.

00:07:17.188 --> 00:07:19.273
The warring factions

00:07:17.188 --> 00:07:19.273
of my kingdom

00:07:19.315 --> 00:07:22.860
are always

00:07:19.315 --> 00:07:22.860
known by the first letter

00:07:19.315 --> 00:07:22.860
of their leader's name.

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:25.196
"W" stands for Wigstan.

00:07:25.237 --> 00:07:26.947
He has royal blood,

00:07:26.989 --> 00:07:30.242
as well as being one

00:07:26.989 --> 00:07:30.242
of the most powerful

00:07:26.989 --> 00:07:30.242
warlords in Mercia.

00:07:30.284 --> 00:07:32.536
Yet he is obviously not

00:07:30.284 --> 00:07:32.536
part of the Ruling Council.

00:07:32.577 --> 00:07:36.456
No. Wigstan would

00:07:32.577 --> 00:07:36.456
find it unbearable

00:07:32.577 --> 00:07:36.456
to belong to any group.

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:39.126
His interests are

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:39.126
always personal.

00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:40.585
Then you don't trust him?

00:07:40.627 --> 00:07:41.962
Trust him?

00:07:42.004 --> 00:07:43.297
(CHUCKLES) My Lord,

00:07:43.339 --> 00:07:45.632
no one should

00:07:43.339 --> 00:07:45.632
ever trust Wigstan!

00:07:45.674 --> 00:07:48.468
So there is

00:07:45.674 --> 00:07:48.468
no dealing with him?

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.222
Absolutely not!

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.222
The only way forward,

00:07:51.263 --> 00:07:53.224
the only choice now,

00:07:53.265 --> 00:07:55.351
is for both of you noble kings

00:07:55.393 --> 00:07:56.935
to raise your armies

00:07:56.977 --> 00:07:58.270
and invade Mercia

00:07:58.312 --> 00:08:00.231
and rid my kingdom

00:08:00.272 --> 00:08:02.607
of all the factions

00:08:00.272 --> 00:08:02.607
who want to ruin me!

00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:04.402
Me!

00:08:04.443 --> 00:08:08.113
The only legitimate ruler

00:08:04.443 --> 00:08:08.113
of that poor, ravaged,

00:08:04.443 --> 00:08:08.113
raped and abused land.

00:08:10.324 --> 00:08:11.409
(SIGHS) I agree

00:08:10.324 --> 00:08:11.409
with the Queen.

00:08:13.285 --> 00:08:15.495
There is no other choice now.

00:08:17.915 --> 00:08:18.916
ECBERT: Huh.

00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:21.585
So it seems.

00:08:22.794 --> 00:08:25.214
Very well.

00:08:22.794 --> 00:08:25.214
We shall take your advice.

00:08:27.925 --> 00:08:29.176
(WHIP SNAPPING)

00:08:33.305 --> 00:08:34.932
(MUTTERING)

00:08:47.111 --> 00:08:48.195
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:08:50.822 --> 00:08:51.907
Wife,

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:54.534
come to bed.

00:08:57.162 --> 00:08:58.497
I said...

00:08:59.664 --> 00:09:00.540
No.

00:09:04.836 --> 00:09:06.004
Why not?

00:09:08.006 --> 00:09:09.174
I don't want to.

00:09:17.433 --> 00:09:19.393
(EXHALES DEEPLY) Very well.

00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:24.606
(VOICE CRACKING)

00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:24.606
Then go sleep with my father,

00:09:25.483 --> 00:09:27.318
(LOUDLY) you whore!

00:09:27.359 --> 00:09:31.155
Yes, yes, and why don't

00:09:27.359 --> 00:09:31.155
you go and sleep

00:09:27.359 --> 00:09:31.155
with your mistress, the Queen.

00:09:31.196 --> 00:09:33.949
Gives you another reason

00:09:31.196 --> 00:09:33.949
to flagellate yourself!

00:09:33.991 --> 00:09:36.160
-(GROANS)

00:09:33.991 --> 00:09:36.160
-Go on. Hit me.

00:09:36.201 --> 00:09:38.870
Hit me if it pleases

00:09:36.201 --> 00:09:38.870
you, husband.

00:09:38.912 --> 00:09:42.582
But it makes no difference,

00:09:38.912 --> 00:09:42.582
either to you or me.

00:09:43.292 --> 00:09:44.793
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

00:09:44.835 --> 00:09:46.586
You are husband to me

00:09:46.628 --> 00:09:50.299
in name only,

00:09:46.628 --> 00:09:50.299
as I am wife to you.

00:09:51.842 --> 00:09:54.886
But you're otherwise free

00:09:51.842 --> 00:09:54.886
to do as you will.

00:09:55.887 --> 00:09:57.597
(SIGHS)

00:09:59.475 --> 00:10:00.559
(SNIFFS)

00:10:02.186 --> 00:10:03.228
(AETHELWULF EXHALING)

00:10:07.899 --> 00:10:09.609
-(EXHALES)

00:10:07.899 --> 00:10:09.609
-(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:10:10.861 --> 00:10:12.363
(DOOR CLOSING)

00:10:20.662 --> 00:10:21.621
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:10:22.998 --> 00:10:24.041
We had an argument.

00:10:24.082 --> 00:10:25.501
Aethelwulf?

00:10:25.543 --> 00:10:27.461
He called me your whore,

00:10:27.503 --> 00:10:29.254
which I am

00:10:29.296 --> 00:10:31.549
and have freely chosen to be.

00:10:36.887 --> 00:10:38.096
Do you want me to leave?

00:10:39.764 --> 00:10:40.640
(HOWLING IN DISTANCE)

00:10:45.812 --> 00:10:47.272
(PAPERS RUSTLING)

00:10:54.279 --> 00:10:56.281
This was my wife's ring.

00:10:57.657 --> 00:11:00.494
My wife died in childbirth.

00:11:00.536 --> 00:11:03.830
I cannot tell

00:11:00.536 --> 00:11:03.830
you the pain of it.

00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:06.250
And I was resolved

00:11:06.291 --> 00:11:07.709
never to marry again.

00:11:08.793 --> 00:11:10.754
But I would like you

00:11:10.795 --> 00:11:11.922
to wear it

00:11:16.427 --> 00:11:17.677
if you will.

00:11:18.929 --> 00:11:22.641
(BELL RINGING)

00:11:31.983 --> 00:11:34.361
I cannot wait to take control

00:11:31.983 --> 00:11:34.361
of my northern lands

00:11:34.403 --> 00:11:35.820
and set up my own court.

00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:38.616
You have some business

00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:38.616
here first, remember?

00:11:38.657 --> 00:11:40.867
Some family business.

00:11:40.909 --> 00:11:42.160
ROLLO: I know.

00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:43.870
A man can dream, can he not,

00:11:43.912 --> 00:11:45.581
of dancing naked on the sand?

00:11:45.623 --> 00:11:48.208
In any case,

00:11:45.623 --> 00:11:48.208
my father needs you.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.379
He needs a strong man

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.379
to support him

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.379
and to guide him.

00:11:52.421 --> 00:11:54.298
(SIGHS) He has Count Odo.

00:11:54.339 --> 00:11:56.007
I don't like Count Odo.

00:11:56.049 --> 00:11:57.426
Nor do I trust him.

00:11:57.968 --> 00:11:59.637
Of course,

00:11:59.678 --> 00:12:01.930
it's possible that he could

00:11:59.678 --> 00:12:01.930
die in the fighting.

00:12:01.972 --> 00:12:04.182
Slain by some

00:12:01.972 --> 00:12:04.182
unknown assailant.

00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:07.018
And then the Emperor

00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:07.018
would just have to

00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:07.018
rely more on you.

00:12:08.186 --> 00:12:10.105
Only a coward

00:12:10.147 --> 00:12:11.523
(INHALES)

00:12:11.565 --> 00:12:13.442
kills a man

00:12:13.484 --> 00:12:15.402
by stabbing him in the back.

00:12:15.444 --> 00:12:17.154
That is what

00:12:15.444 --> 00:12:17.154
a Viking would say.

00:12:17.195 --> 00:12:19.490
But you are no

00:12:17.195 --> 00:12:19.490
longer a Viking.

00:12:19.531 --> 00:12:22.784
In Frankia, we do

00:12:19.531 --> 00:12:22.784
certain things differently.

00:12:22.826 --> 00:12:26.037
That is something you'll

00:12:22.826 --> 00:12:26.037
have to learn, my love.

00:12:26.079 --> 00:12:28.666
(CHUCKLES) Something you'll

00:12:26.079 --> 00:12:28.666
certainly have to learn.

00:12:30.208 --> 00:12:31.751
(BELLS RINGING IN DISTANCE)

00:12:37.299 --> 00:12:38.842
(MEN TALKING SOFTLY)

00:12:46.183 --> 00:12:47.351
(DOORS CLOSING)

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.524
CHARLES: You asked

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.524
for a private audience.

00:12:57.736 --> 00:12:59.070
Why?

00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:01.156
Your Highness, forgive me,

00:13:01.198 --> 00:13:05.910
I am reluctant to discuss

00:13:01.198 --> 00:13:05.910
matters which relate

00:13:01.198 --> 00:13:05.910
directly to my superior.

00:13:05.952 --> 00:13:07.329
CHARLES: You mean Count Odo?

00:13:09.164 --> 00:13:11.791
Then absolve

00:13:09.164 --> 00:13:11.791
yourself of any guilt

00:13:11.833 --> 00:13:14.002
and just say what

00:13:11.833 --> 00:13:14.002
you have to say.

00:13:14.044 --> 00:13:15.754
Highness, I am troubled

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:17.797
that you always

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:17.797
trust his word.

00:13:18.674 --> 00:13:20.800
Why?

00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:24.179
Should... Should I not

00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:24.179
trust his word?

00:13:24.221 --> 00:13:27.349
Because he is not

00:13:24.221 --> 00:13:27.349
always worth believing.

00:13:27.391 --> 00:13:30.602
Why, pray,

00:13:27.391 --> 00:13:30.602
is he not worth believing?

00:13:30.644 --> 00:13:32.688
Because he is ambitious.

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:35.982
Ambitious beyond ambitious.

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:40.070
So that even an Emperor's

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:40.070
crown would not sit

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:40.070
untidily upon his head.

00:13:42.113 --> 00:13:44.115
(BIRDS SHRIEKING IN DISTANCE)

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.748
An Emperor's crown?

00:13:56.086 --> 00:13:57.045
I cannot believe it!

00:13:58.171 --> 00:14:00.799
What... What are you saying?

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.426
(SHOUTING) Do...

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.426
Do you have any proof of this?

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:03.385
I have the word

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:03.385
of his mistress.

00:14:05.303 --> 00:14:06.971
And, as your Highness knows,

00:14:07.013 --> 00:14:10.100
a man will always

00:14:07.013 --> 00:14:10.100
divulge the truth

00:14:07.013 --> 00:14:10.100
first to his mistress,

00:14:10.768 --> 00:14:12.227
and only afterwards,

00:14:12.269 --> 00:14:13.353
if at all,

00:14:13.395 --> 00:14:14.813
to his wife.

00:14:15.564 --> 00:14:16.898
Very well.

00:14:18.066 --> 00:14:20.778
Let me talk to his mistress.

00:14:20.819 --> 00:14:22.696
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:14:31.705 --> 00:14:33.457
CHARLES: For God's sake!

00:14:33.498 --> 00:14:35.459
How should I

00:14:33.498 --> 00:14:35.459
trust the evidence

00:14:33.498 --> 00:14:35.459
of this woman?

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.254
Because this

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.254
woman is my sister.

00:14:45.969 --> 00:14:47.304
CHARLES: Is it true?

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.598
THERESE: Yes, Your Highness.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.015
And?

00:14:51.057 --> 00:14:56.647
Does Count Odo talk

00:14:51.057 --> 00:14:56.647
freely of his ambitions?

00:14:57.606 --> 00:14:58.898
Yes, he does.

00:14:59.691 --> 00:15:00.734
Very freely.

00:15:05.322 --> 00:15:06.615
His ambition

00:15:06.657 --> 00:15:08.908
(STUTTERING) to replace me?

00:15:12.162 --> 00:15:13.664
To become

00:15:14.748 --> 00:15:15.915
Emperor?

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.168
Yes, exactly.

00:15:19.586 --> 00:15:23.173
His ambition

00:15:19.586 --> 00:15:23.173
to become Emperor.

00:15:23.799 --> 00:15:24.800
Then...

00:15:25.884 --> 00:15:27.427
Then I beg you,

00:15:29.387 --> 00:15:30.639
(STUTTERING) please,

00:15:30.681 --> 00:15:31.807
stay close

00:15:31.849 --> 00:15:33.851
to Count Odo.

00:15:33.892 --> 00:15:37.855
Report to me

00:15:33.892 --> 00:15:37.855
anything which might

00:15:33.892 --> 00:15:37.855
signal his treachery.

00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:41.608
Now, go! Leave me!

00:15:47.865 --> 00:15:49.949
(SOBBING IN DISTANCE)

00:15:56.373 --> 00:15:59.376
(CHUCKLES)

00:15:59.417 --> 00:16:02.170
ODO: The forts have been

00:15:59.417 --> 00:16:02.170
built according to your

00:15:59.417 --> 00:16:02.170
instructions, Your Grace.

00:16:02.212 --> 00:16:04.130
Eventually there will be

00:16:02.212 --> 00:16:04.130
an iron chain

00:16:04.172 --> 00:16:05.340
which can be raised

00:16:04.172 --> 00:16:05.340
between them

00:16:05.382 --> 00:16:07.050
to prevent the passage

00:16:05.382 --> 00:16:07.050
of any boat upriver.

00:16:07.091 --> 00:16:08.927
We should still place

00:16:07.091 --> 00:16:08.927
some boats beyond

00:16:07.091 --> 00:16:08.927
this barrier,

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:10.804
in case they break through.

00:16:10.846 --> 00:16:12.890
Hopefully, they will be

00:16:10.846 --> 00:16:12.890
unable to do so.

00:16:12.931 --> 00:16:15.266
You don't know

00:16:12.931 --> 00:16:15.266
my people like I do.

00:16:15.308 --> 00:16:16.935
They don't recognize

00:16:15.308 --> 00:16:16.935
any barriers,

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:18.854
except as obstacles

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:18.854
to be overcome.

00:16:18.896 --> 00:16:21.857
What has become clear

00:16:18.896 --> 00:16:21.857
to both the Emperor

00:16:18.896 --> 00:16:21.857
and myself

00:16:21.899 --> 00:16:24.902
is that, if we were

00:16:21.899 --> 00:16:24.902
to lose Paris,

00:16:21.899 --> 00:16:24.902
we would lose everything.

00:16:24.943 --> 00:16:26.945
For then the enemy

00:16:24.943 --> 00:16:26.945
would command

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:28.530
the Marne, the Seine

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:28.530
and the Yonne rivers,

00:16:28.572 --> 00:16:30.448
and the country would lie open

00:16:28.572 --> 00:16:30.448
as far as Rheims.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.951
We must hold Paris

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.951
whatever the cost.

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:36.580
There is no alternative.

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:36.580
No other choice.

00:16:36.621 --> 00:16:39.499
When my brother returns,

00:16:36.621 --> 00:16:39.499
everything will be

00:16:36.621 --> 00:16:39.499
decided here.

00:16:53.597 --> 00:16:55.014
(BIRD CHITTERING)

00:16:57.893 --> 00:16:58.894
(SIGHS)

00:17:06.443 --> 00:17:07.318
(CHITTERING CONTINUES)

00:17:11.489 --> 00:17:12.657
Is this how you looked?

00:17:14.117 --> 00:17:15.076
Yes.

00:17:17.704 --> 00:17:19.748
Though my hair

00:17:17.704 --> 00:17:19.748
was much shorter.

00:17:24.252 --> 00:17:26.838
What is the name

00:17:24.252 --> 00:17:26.838
of your kingdom?

00:17:28.089 --> 00:17:29.048
China.

00:17:30.091 --> 00:17:31.342
And who rules it?

00:17:32.636 --> 00:17:34.596
The Emperor Dezong,

00:17:34.638 --> 00:17:36.222
of the Tang Dynasty.

00:17:40.393 --> 00:17:42.061
I want to know

00:17:40.393 --> 00:17:42.061
about your father.

00:17:43.939 --> 00:17:46.149
My father was a... A merchant.

00:17:46.733 --> 00:17:48.192
Well respected.

00:17:49.152 --> 00:17:51.655
Rich enough to own a boat.

00:17:51.696 --> 00:17:52.781
What about the Emperor?

00:17:52.823 --> 00:17:54.240
Tell me about him.

00:17:55.909 --> 00:17:57.911
The Emperor had

00:17:55.909 --> 00:17:57.911
many daughters...

00:17:57.953 --> 00:17:59.245
Mmm.

00:17:59.287 --> 00:18:01.748
...with his wives

00:17:59.287 --> 00:18:01.748
and concubines.

00:18:03.041 --> 00:18:05.543
His concubines

00:18:03.041 --> 00:18:05.543
were looked after

00:18:05.585 --> 00:18:06.920
by the palace eunuchs.

00:18:08.005 --> 00:18:09.088
Eunuchs?

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:11.090
Men who are not men.

00:18:13.092 --> 00:18:14.594
Why are they not men?

00:18:14.636 --> 00:18:18.015
Their manhood was cut off,

00:18:18.056 --> 00:18:21.351
so they could not

00:18:18.056 --> 00:18:21.351
have sex with the Emperor's

00:18:18.056 --> 00:18:21.351
wives or slaves.

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:25.355
I don't like that.

00:18:25.689 --> 00:18:26.815
No.

00:18:26.857 --> 00:18:28.608
They didn't like it either.

00:18:32.029 --> 00:18:33.530
(YIDU SNICKERS)

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.534
(CHUCKLES)

00:18:44.374 --> 00:18:46.043
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:18:56.845 --> 00:18:58.596
(WHISPERS) Are you one

00:18:56.845 --> 00:18:58.596
of the Emperor's daughters?

00:19:00.015 --> 00:19:01.140
(EXHALES)

00:19:09.482 --> 00:19:12.151
-My father was a merchant.

00:19:09.482 --> 00:19:12.151
-I know.

00:19:12.193 --> 00:19:13.528
You told me that before.

00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:18.783
I don't know you.

00:19:19.784 --> 00:19:21.578
And you don't know me.

00:19:21.619 --> 00:19:25.790
Yet I want to tell you

00:19:21.619 --> 00:19:25.790
my most terrible secret.

00:19:26.666 --> 00:19:28.585
-Do you want to hear it?

00:19:26.666 --> 00:19:28.585
-Yes.

00:19:28.626 --> 00:19:29.920
Mmm-hmm?

00:19:31.796 --> 00:19:33.715
I can share your burden.

00:19:33.757 --> 00:19:35.174
Mmm.

00:19:35.592 --> 00:19:36.885
I am small,

00:19:36.927 --> 00:19:39.178
but I have broad shoulders

00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:41.765
and I am not afraid.

00:19:44.392 --> 00:19:47.186
I will tell you

00:19:44.392 --> 00:19:47.186
when you tell me the truth

00:19:44.392 --> 00:19:47.186
about your father.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.067
-(GRUNTS)

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.067
-(GASPS)

00:19:52.817 --> 00:19:54.193
All right.

00:19:55.779 --> 00:19:57.363
Then give me

00:19:55.779 --> 00:19:57.363
more of that medicine.

00:20:10.585 --> 00:20:12.211
(BIRD CHITTERING)

00:20:22.931 --> 00:20:24.557
(CHOPPING)

00:20:28.979 --> 00:20:30.229
-(HORN BLOWING)

00:20:28.979 --> 00:20:30.229
-(CHATTERING)

00:20:33.108 --> 00:20:34.818
Bjorn Ironside,

00:20:34.859 --> 00:20:36.235
come and sit with me.

00:20:43.034 --> 00:20:44.452
We should talk to one another.

00:20:48.123 --> 00:20:50.000
You don't trust me.

00:20:50.041 --> 00:20:52.418
I have no reason to trust you.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.129
You have told me

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.129
of your ambitions.

00:20:55.296 --> 00:20:56.881
Whether my ambitions

00:20:55.296 --> 00:20:56.881
come true or not,

00:20:56.923 --> 00:20:58.091
it's not up to me.

00:20:58.842 --> 00:21:00.760
As well you know.

00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:02.179
'Cause I can

00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:02.179
make sure they don't.

00:21:04.014 --> 00:21:05.015
(SNIFFS)

00:21:07.308 --> 00:21:09.519
I will never give you

00:21:07.308 --> 00:21:09.519
any cause to kill me.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.436
(SCOFFS)

00:21:12.022 --> 00:21:14.398
That is not for you to say.

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:16.275
I may find cause

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:16.275
where others may not.

00:21:17.694 --> 00:21:18.653
Who knows?

00:21:20.947 --> 00:21:22.448
(DRUM MUSIC STARTS PLAYING)

00:21:24.909 --> 00:21:26.619
But for now anyway,

00:21:27.829 --> 00:21:29.122
we are allies.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:34.502
And we shall go

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:34.502
together to Paris.

00:21:34.544 --> 00:21:37.005
And we shall fight together.

00:21:34.544 --> 00:21:37.005
Is it not so?

00:21:38.631 --> 00:21:42.301
You and Ragnar need

00:21:38.631 --> 00:21:42.301
my warriors.

00:21:38.631 --> 00:21:42.301
You need my ships.

00:21:44.595 --> 00:21:46.264
I can't wait for Paris,

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:47.891
Bjorn Ironside.

00:21:47.932 --> 00:21:49.308
I cannot wait.

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:52.311
We shall destroy

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:52.311
those Christian folk!

00:21:52.353 --> 00:21:54.605
They have seen nothing yet.

00:21:54.647 --> 00:21:56.274
We are the masters now!

00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:58.109
-Is it not so?

00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:58.109
-ALL MEN: Yes! Yeah!

00:21:58.151 --> 00:22:00.278
-Is it not so?

00:21:58.151 --> 00:22:00.278
-ALL MEN: Yes!

00:22:06.951 --> 00:22:08.327
AELLE: So we are agreed,

00:22:08.369 --> 00:22:10.914
we'll raise an army

00:22:08.369 --> 00:22:10.914
and attack Mercia.

00:22:10.955 --> 00:22:12.790
There is no alternative,

00:22:10.955 --> 00:22:12.790
my Lord Aelle.

00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:15.585
Not if we wish to see Queen

00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:15.585
Kwenthrith placed once

00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:15.585
more upon the throne.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:17.921
(HORSES NEIGHING)

00:22:17.962 --> 00:22:19.422
Travel safely, my Lord.

00:22:19.463 --> 00:22:22.259
You are the best of allies.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:24.052
AELLE: I'm a simple

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:24.052
man at heart,

00:22:24.094 --> 00:22:27.346
-but full of conviction.

00:22:24.094 --> 00:22:27.346
-ECBERT: Your convictions,

00:22:24.094 --> 00:22:27.346
do you credit.

00:22:29.348 --> 00:22:31.059
Farewell, my child.

00:22:33.811 --> 00:22:35.188
Take heed

00:22:33.811 --> 00:22:35.188
of what I've told you.

00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:38.858
I will always

00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:38.858
listen to you, Father.

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:42.361
But also to my own conscience,

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:42.361
and weigh such things in the

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:42.361
balance, as it pleases you.

00:22:42.403 --> 00:22:44.781
It does not always please me.

00:22:44.822 --> 00:22:46.241
But enough!

00:22:46.283 --> 00:22:47.366
Women are frail.

00:22:48.492 --> 00:22:49.368
Farewell, children.

00:22:50.954 --> 00:22:53.414
Remember your duties,

00:22:50.954 --> 00:22:53.414
say your prayers,

00:22:53.456 --> 00:22:55.792
and banish the Devil

00:22:53.456 --> 00:22:55.792
from your thoughts.

00:22:55.833 --> 00:22:57.376
Such good advice,

00:22:55.833 --> 00:22:57.376
my Lord Aelle.

00:22:58.461 --> 00:22:59.378
Farewell.

00:23:02.006 --> 00:23:03.466
KWENTHRITH: King Ecbert?

00:23:03.507 --> 00:23:04.592
MAN: Front King's Guard!

00:23:04.634 --> 00:23:07.053
-Yes, Queen Kwenthrith?

00:23:04.634 --> 00:23:07.053
-MAN: All men forward!

00:23:07.845 --> 00:23:09.139
MAN: Move out!

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:11.390
I need to know

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:11.390
that I can trust you.

00:23:11.432 --> 00:23:13.351
That you will do

00:23:11.432 --> 00:23:13.351
what you promised me.

00:23:13.392 --> 00:23:14.602
Why would you doubt me?

00:23:16.271 --> 00:23:19.565
You've heard me speak

00:23:16.271 --> 00:23:19.565
plainly and in public.

00:23:19.607 --> 00:23:21.985
I doubt you

00:23:19.607 --> 00:23:21.985
for one reason only.

00:23:22.026 --> 00:23:25.571
And that is that you and I are

00:23:22.026 --> 00:23:25.571
somewhat alike.

00:23:26.781 --> 00:23:29.408
Then do not judge

00:23:26.781 --> 00:23:29.408
yourself too harshly.

00:23:31.869 --> 00:23:32.620
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:23:37.834 --> 00:23:38.626
(DOOR CREAK OPEN)

00:23:53.016 --> 00:23:54.100
Lord,

00:23:58.021 --> 00:23:59.522
you know me for a sinner.

00:24:04.194 --> 00:24:05.444
My sins are

00:24:07.405 --> 00:24:10.449
carnal, venal,

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:14.495
and unforgivable.

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:14.495
I know that.

00:24:18.208 --> 00:24:21.627
And I think you have

00:24:18.208 --> 00:24:21.627
already decided

00:24:21.669 --> 00:24:23.587
to cast me out

00:24:21.669 --> 00:24:23.587
into the darkness,

00:24:24.714 --> 00:24:25.756
like a fallen angel,

00:24:27.175 --> 00:24:29.635
to suffer in purgatory,

00:24:27.175 --> 00:24:29.635
or the fires of hell,

00:24:29.677 --> 00:24:31.346
for all eternity.

00:24:35.933 --> 00:24:37.143
Think you, Lord,

00:24:38.853 --> 00:24:41.398
that I can look upon such

00:24:38.853 --> 00:24:41.398
scenes with equanimity?

00:24:43.649 --> 00:24:45.818
That I do not dream,

00:24:43.649 --> 00:24:45.818
in the dead of night,

00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:48.405
of returning to your light

00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:48.405
and the promises of heaven?

00:24:48.446 --> 00:24:50.698
Am I not a man

00:24:48.446 --> 00:24:50.698
like other men?

00:24:57.788 --> 00:24:58.706
And yet,

00:25:00.583 --> 00:25:02.835
I would sup with the Devil

00:25:02.877 --> 00:25:04.128
if he would show me

00:25:04.170 --> 00:25:06.505
how to achieve

00:25:04.170 --> 00:25:06.505
my earthly goals.

00:25:06.547 --> 00:25:09.384
Your kingdom, Lord,

00:25:06.547 --> 00:25:09.384
as you have said,

00:25:09.426 --> 00:25:11.969
is not of this world,

00:25:12.011 --> 00:25:14.305
but my kingdom is.

00:25:20.978 --> 00:25:22.146
And therefore,

00:25:24.148 --> 00:25:26.525
there is no help for me.

00:25:28.611 --> 00:25:31.281
No other way for me

00:25:34.867 --> 00:25:36.786
but eternal damnation.

00:25:54.845 --> 00:25:55.763
(GROANS)

00:26:06.149 --> 00:26:07.650
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

00:26:11.737 --> 00:26:13.156
(HORNS BLOWING)

00:26:23.374 --> 00:26:24.959
MAN 1: A boat's come in!

00:26:23.374 --> 00:26:24.959
MAN 2: They're here!

00:26:27.628 --> 00:26:30.423
MAN 3: Bring him in!

00:26:27.628 --> 00:26:30.423
MAN 4: Over here!

00:26:32.008 --> 00:26:32.842
(TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

00:26:34.885 --> 00:26:36.513
(CHEERING)

00:26:37.054 --> 00:26:38.139
(BOTH GRUNTING)

00:26:40.016 --> 00:26:41.142
-Brother.

00:26:40.016 --> 00:26:41.142
-Brother!

00:26:44.562 --> 00:26:45.813
This is Kattegat!

00:26:45.855 --> 00:26:47.648
This is Kattegat.

00:26:50.067 --> 00:26:51.068
Come.

00:26:52.445 --> 00:26:53.446
(KNIFE THUDS)

00:26:56.032 --> 00:26:56.782
(KNIFE THUDS)

00:26:59.869 --> 00:27:00.703
King Ragnar,

00:27:03.289 --> 00:27:05.542
this is my brother Halfdan.

00:27:07.043 --> 00:27:09.462
Meet the notorious

00:27:07.043 --> 00:27:09.462
King Ragnar.

00:27:09.504 --> 00:27:10.547
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:27:12.382 --> 00:27:13.632
HALFDAN: It's a great honor.

00:27:16.677 --> 00:27:18.012
When do we sail for Paris?

00:27:19.514 --> 00:27:20.848
LOTHBROK:

00:27:19.514 --> 00:27:20.848
You seem eager to fight.

00:27:20.890 --> 00:27:23.351
HALFDAN: Yes, it's true.

00:27:23.393 --> 00:27:25.728
Not just

00:27:23.393 --> 00:27:25.728
for the sake of fighting,

00:27:23.393 --> 00:27:25.728
but for the beauty of it.

00:27:31.817 --> 00:27:33.570
And against

00:27:31.817 --> 00:27:33.570
the Christians, yes.

00:27:33.611 --> 00:27:35.696
I hate the Christians.

00:27:35.738 --> 00:27:37.073
In the name of Odin,

00:27:35.738 --> 00:27:37.073
I would kill them all.

00:27:38.991 --> 00:27:41.035
You'll have the opportunity

00:27:38.991 --> 00:27:41.035
to kill a great number of them

00:27:43.829 --> 00:27:44.872
once we reach Paris.

00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:49.210
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:27:49.252 --> 00:27:50.669
(KNIVES THUDDING)

00:28:03.682 --> 00:28:05.643
-(CHEERING AND LAUGHING)

00:28:03.682 --> 00:28:05.643
-WOMAN: Faster!

00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:07.103
-Argh!

00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:07.103
-(LAUGHING)

00:28:07.144 --> 00:28:08.729
(DRUMS PLAYING)

00:28:11.274 --> 00:28:13.692
(SHOUTING AND LAUGHING)

00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:34.713
(SHOUTING AND

00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:34.713
LAUGHING CONTINUES)

00:28:39.760 --> 00:28:41.387
They'll be wondering

00:28:39.760 --> 00:28:41.387
where you are.

00:28:43.931 --> 00:28:45.015
I doubt it.

00:28:55.568 --> 00:28:56.902
(SIGHS)

00:29:10.040 --> 00:29:11.917
What are you thinking about?

00:29:11.959 --> 00:29:12.835
Paris.

00:29:14.962 --> 00:29:18.090
You must be excited

00:29:14.962 --> 00:29:18.090
to be going back.

00:29:18.132 --> 00:29:19.216
(SOFTLY) No.

00:29:23.929 --> 00:29:24.930
I feel so old.

00:29:29.810 --> 00:29:32.396
When I was young,

00:29:29.810 --> 00:29:32.396
I had the passion to win,

00:29:32.438 --> 00:29:36.942
but now, with age

00:29:32.438 --> 00:29:36.942
and all that comes with it,

00:29:38.902 --> 00:29:40.363
I have lost the desire.

00:29:42.490 --> 00:29:43.700
And the strength.

00:29:56.086 --> 00:29:58.339
A few years ago

00:29:56.086 --> 00:29:58.339
I established a settlement

00:29:58.381 --> 00:30:02.343
in a distant country

00:29:58.381 --> 00:30:02.343
where I took many

00:29:58.381 --> 00:30:02.343
of my people and friends

00:30:02.385 --> 00:30:04.554
to make a new life

00:30:02.385 --> 00:30:04.554
for themselves.

00:30:08.766 --> 00:30:11.352
But shortly after

00:30:08.766 --> 00:30:11.352
my departure,

00:30:08.766 --> 00:30:11.352
they were all slaughtered.

00:30:11.394 --> 00:30:13.563
Their homes

00:30:11.394 --> 00:30:13.563
destroyed and burned.

00:30:16.399 --> 00:30:17.816
I live with such guilt

00:30:16.399 --> 00:30:17.816
because of it.

00:30:19.276 --> 00:30:20.778
(INHALES DEEPLY)

00:30:22.029 --> 00:30:23.531
(SIGHS)

00:30:26.784 --> 00:30:28.118
And nobody knows.

00:30:45.928 --> 00:30:47.722
My father's the Emperor.

00:30:51.475 --> 00:30:52.851
(LAUGHS)

00:31:04.321 --> 00:31:06.240
-(SHOUTING AND LAUGHING)

00:31:04.321 --> 00:31:06.240
-(MUSIC CONTINUES)

00:31:14.665 --> 00:31:18.586
They say he left Kattegat

00:31:14.665 --> 00:31:18.586
a boy and came back a man.

00:31:19.837 --> 00:31:21.297
Killed a bear

00:31:19.837 --> 00:31:21.297
with his bare hands.

00:31:22.506 --> 00:31:23.591
With his own hands?

00:31:23.924 --> 00:31:24.883
Hmm.

00:31:26.885 --> 00:31:27.886
(MUSIC STOPS)

00:31:33.142 --> 00:31:34.560
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:31:41.317 --> 00:31:43.319
Who is that?

00:31:43.360 --> 00:31:44.903
It is Floki, the boat builder.

00:31:45.946 --> 00:31:47.948
For some reason,

00:31:45.946 --> 00:31:47.948
no one will tell me

00:31:47.990 --> 00:31:49.408
he has fallen out

00:31:47.990 --> 00:31:49.408
with King Ragnar.

00:31:50.284 --> 00:31:51.285
Ask him.

00:31:52.703 --> 00:31:54.831
HALFDAN: Floki.

00:31:52.703 --> 00:31:54.831
Boat builder.

00:31:54.872 --> 00:31:55.914
Sit down with us.

00:31:56.833 --> 00:31:58.917
Yes, Floki. Sit down.

00:31:56.833 --> 00:31:58.917
Make room.

00:32:05.174 --> 00:32:06.509
Both of you join us.

00:32:06.550 --> 00:32:07.885
-Fill the horns.

00:32:06.550 --> 00:32:07.885
-Sup.

00:32:07.926 --> 00:32:10.304
This is

00:32:07.926 --> 00:32:10.304
my younger brother, Halfdan.

00:32:11.848 --> 00:32:13.557
-He's keen to know you.

00:32:11.848 --> 00:32:13.557
-All right.

00:32:18.312 --> 00:32:21.816
So, you are the genius

00:32:18.312 --> 00:32:21.816
that built the boats

00:32:18.312 --> 00:32:21.816
that changed our world,

00:32:21.858 --> 00:32:24.318
and helped made Ragnar

00:32:21.858 --> 00:32:24.318
so famous!

00:32:24.360 --> 00:32:27.154
Why would he fall out

00:32:24.360 --> 00:32:27.154
with someone like you?

00:32:27.196 --> 00:32:28.947
Because I killed

00:32:27.196 --> 00:32:28.947
his pet Christian.

00:32:28.989 --> 00:32:29.948
-Floki!

00:32:28.989 --> 00:32:29.948
-(CHUCKLES)

00:32:32.242 --> 00:32:33.076
Skol.

00:32:34.620 --> 00:32:35.746
To new friendships.

00:32:36.246 --> 00:32:37.414
Skol!

00:32:38.040 --> 00:32:39.375
Skol!

00:32:39.416 --> 00:32:40.292
(SOFTLY) Skol.

00:32:51.387 --> 00:32:52.638
(EXHALES)

00:33:22.626 --> 00:33:23.669
(EXHALES)

00:33:40.686 --> 00:33:41.979
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:33:59.329 --> 00:34:00.330
(GASPS)

00:34:21.602 --> 00:34:22.645
(SHUDDERS)

00:34:35.574 --> 00:34:36.909
(MOANS SOFTLY)

00:34:43.624 --> 00:34:45.083
(MOANS SOFTLY)

00:35:39.638 --> 00:35:41.139
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:35:46.436 --> 00:35:47.855
(MOANS)

00:36:09.334 --> 00:36:10.711
